    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Six little elephants, A, B, C, D, E, F, are lining up to buy tickets. F is after A and before D and he is also between B and C; B is the first in the line; and E is the last in the line. Which elephant is F?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "the 2nd"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "the 3rd"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "the 4th"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "the 5th"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "the 6th"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Build the line",
        "body": "B is 1st and E is 6th. The middle places 2, 3, 4, 5 are for A, C, D, F.\n\n- F is between B and C, so C comes after F.\n- F is after A, so A comes before F.\n- F is before D.\n\nSo A is the only one of A, C, D before F: the line is B, A, F, then C and D. F is **3rd**.\n\n**Answer: (B) the 3rd**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Count who is in front",
        "body": "In front of F are exactly B and A (C, D and E are all behind F). Two elephants in front means F is 3rd.\n\n**Answer: (B) the 3rd**"
      }
    ],
