        "body": "Gear A has **7 teeth**. When it makes one full turn, 7 teeth pass the meeting point, so each of the other gears also turns by 7 teeth.\n\n- Gear A turns clockwise, so the middle gear turns anticlockwise and the right gear turns **clockwise** again.\n- The right gear has **6 teeth**. Turning by 7 teeth is one full turn (6 teeth) plus 1 more tooth.\n\nSo x ends up one tooth further clockwise than where it started. x started at the bottom-right tooth (where b is), and one tooth clockwise from there is the bottom-left tooth, labelled **a**.\n\n**Answer: (A) a**"
      }
    ],
